WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.000
-We're about to play
"Hey Robot."

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:07.601
-♪ Hey, hey, robot ♪

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.467
♪ Hey, robot ♪

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.501
-I'm going to need some help,
so joining me now

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:14.067
is the star of the new film
"Nightmare Alley,"

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.334
which is in theaters now.

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:18.133
Please welcome the one and only
Cate Blanchett!

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:21.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.534
[ Laughs ]

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.834
Cate, here's how the game works.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.868
Okay, this is based on a real
board game called "Hey Robot"

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:28.968
that you can play at home.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.901
It's like the classic game
"Password,"

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.033
but your partner is
a smart speaker.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.634
Okay, so first, I will pick
a card with a word on it,

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:39.200
and then we'll take turns --
-That looks like a sex aid.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:43.634
That doesn't look like --
What is that?

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:47.167
I know I'm on Zoom,
but what is that?

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.133
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.067
It's not --
Your kids can see this.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:53.234
This is totally --
This is a smart speaker.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.968
-Okay.
-This is a smart speaker.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.734
-A "smart speaker."
-That's correct.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.601
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, whatever.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.801
-I'll pick a card
with a word on it.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.434
[ Laughs ]
-Okay.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:05.634
-And we are going to take turns
asking a question, okay?

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.467
And all we want is
to get the speaker

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.567
to say that word
somewhere in its answer.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.267
Okay?
And if it does, you get a point.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.934
We can't say the word,
obviously.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:16.267
Okay? I'll start. You'll see.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.767
Here we go.
-Okay.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.167
-Alright, here we go.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:25.067
Oh. Alright, so, I have to get
it to say the word "rubber."

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.133
Okay.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:32.434
Alexa, what are tires made of?

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.567
-Here's something I found
on the web.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:38.467
According to servicecity.com,
the main materials

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.834
for the production of tires
are rubber, which is --

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.300
[ Ding! ]

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.701
-I don't know if I'm going to
make it through the whole game.

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:02.334
-This has nothing to do with
the "smart speaker."

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:06.934
This has to do with --
This is the Olympiad, isn't it?

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.534
-That's exactly right.
-I'm meant to do some sort of

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:13.434
physical, active --
my physical prowess --

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.667
-That's correct. Exactly.
New Year's resolution.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.934
Yeah, even if you --
So, you're up.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:20.834
And you have to get the smart
speaker, which is what it is,

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:24.033
to say the word "mushrooms."

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:37.467
-Apar-- Alexa, apart from beef,
what is in beef Stroganoff?

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.033
-Here is what I found.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.133
According to cooksinfo.com,

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.968
beef Stroganoff is a dish
consisting of thin slices

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.834
of cooked beef
and sliced mushrooms.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.434
[ Ding! ]
-Oh, come on!

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:49.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.200
Yes!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.901
You're good.

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.367
We got to take this on the road!

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:54.801
Oh! Oh, my God!

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:55.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.834 --> 00:03:00.467
Oh, my God!
[ Laughing ]

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:03.834
It is my turn again.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.100
Unfortunately, I have to get it
to say -- Oh.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:10.200
"Walrus."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.234
Alright.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.734
The walrus was...

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.300
Alright.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:21.667
Alexa, according to the Beatles,
who was Paul?

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.601
-Here's what I found
from the Web.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.234
Sir Paul McCartney has been
hailed as a genius

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:31.400
by St. Vincent for his work
with the new remix of his song.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.634
The Beatles legend asked
39-year-old Annie Clark,

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:37.901
real name Annie Clark, to appear
in the remix of his song

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.534
"Women and Wives," from this
year's "McCartney III Imagined"

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:43.534
compilation, which features
a new version of his song.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.767
Was that helpful?
-No.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.100
No, that wasn't --
-Thanks for your feedback.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.167
-Yeah, you're welcome.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.634
That wasn't helpful.
Now it is your turn,

00:03:57.634 --> 00:04:00.601
my partner, Cate,
whenever you're ready.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.400
-Oh, gosh.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.634
Alexa, in Lewis Carroll's
"Alice in Wonderland,"

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.200
who was on the beach?

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.100
-Sorry, I don't have
an answer for that.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.834
-Oh, well, that's not
my problem.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.501
-Let me start. Let me say it.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:21.167
-Alexa, according to Lewis
Carroll's "Alice in Wonderland,"

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:22.667
who was on the beach?

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.767
-Here's something I found
on the web.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:28.200
According to sea.edu,
on the beach,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.167
terror strikes Robinson Crusoe,

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:33.534
the first of many castaways to
confront destiny on the sand.

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:35.033
-Yep.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.434
[ Laughter ]
-This is going well.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.234
-That's fantastic.
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.400
Ready? Here we go. Ready?

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.267
Alexa, what are the top three
animals with tusks?

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:49.701
-According to an Alexa answers
contributor, elephants.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.267
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.734
-So close.
I'm skipping that one, okay?

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:01.601
-Okay, one more.
-Alright, try one more.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.300
Here we go. This is it.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:10.334
-Alexa, can you name an animal
with tusks that begins with W?

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.367
-Sorry, I don't know that.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:14.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:16.067
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:17.734
-Ah, nice try.

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.300
[ Laughs ]

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.667
What?
-She knows even less than I do.

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.567
-She's like, "I don't know --
welephant?"

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:23.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:25.133
Alright, here we go.

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.734
The last one, let's make this
work, here we go.

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:30.334
Alright, I have to make
the smart speaker say...

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.734
"oink."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:34.534
I think I can do this, right?

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:39.534
Alexa, what sound does
a pig make?

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:41.901
-Okay. Here's animal noises.

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:44.033
A pig goes --
[ Pig oinking ]

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.267
[ Laughter ]
Which would you like next?

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:48.133
-Does that count, judges?

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:49.167
[ Dinging ]

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:50.634
That's it, we did it! Alright!

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.634
Cate Blanchett!

